#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-02.png", width: 471.5pt), 60.5pt, 86.5pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "bold", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(42.6pt, 241.08pt, "2.1.")
  #line-at(58.56pt, 241.08pt, "Air clad ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(51.6pt, 253.2pt, "A simple yet efficient waveguide is a ribbon waveguide. Owing to ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 263.64pt, "the etching process, the cross-section of the waveguide has a ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 273.96pt, "rectangular shape. Since the silicon core has high refractive index ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 284.4pt, "(")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 284.4pt, "𝑛≈3.4")
  #line-at(74.4pt, 284.4pt, ") and is cladded by air with low index (")
  #line-at(216.84pt, 284.4pt, "𝑛= 1")
  #line-at(238.92pt, 284.4pt, "), the wave is ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 294.84pt, "strongly confined by TIR in both in-plane (")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(199.08pt, 294.84pt, "x-z")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(209.52pt, 294.84pt, ") and out-of-plane (")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(280.2pt, 294.84pt, "y-")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 305.16pt, "z")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(46.08pt, 305.16pt, ") directions. A number of silicon ribbon waveguides developed for ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 315.6pt, "frequency bands from 100 GHz up to 1 THz with high transmittances ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 325.92pt, "have been reported [4]. Since the bare guiding channel has a small ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 336.36pt, "cross-section (<1")
  #line-at(105.96pt, 336.36pt, "×")
  #line-at(112.44pt, 336.36pt, " 1 mm")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(134.64pt, 333.36pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(137.64pt, 336.36pt, " for sub-THz bands) without supporting ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 346.8pt, "structures, it is impractical to manipulate the waveguide for ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 357.12pt, "accommodating with other components. Therefore, tethered frame ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 367.44pt, "or low-index claddings are introduced. However, these claddings ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 377.88pt, "will also cause the wave interference to the structure, and there will ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 388.2pt, "be a trade-off between the transmittance and physical strength of the ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 398.52pt, "waveguide [7], [8]. In addition to silicon, 3D-printed alumina is a ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 408.84pt, "promising technology, as the relative permittivity of materials can be ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 419.28pt, "arbitrarily controlled [9]. ")
  #line-at(51.6pt, 432.6pt, "It is worth noting that a pair of metallic hollow-waveguide ports ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 442.92pt, "are attached to both ends of each silicon waveguide to excite the ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 453.24pt, "fundamental TE (transverse-electric) or TM (transverse-magnetic) ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 463.68pt, "mode. In order to mitigate impedance mismatch between the metal ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 474pt, "waveguide and the silicon core, tapered spikes are incorporated at ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 484.32pt, "both terminations of the dielectric waveguides. These tapers ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 494.64pt, "gradually modify the effective refractive index and modal field ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 505.08pt, "distribution, thereby reducing reflection at the interface and allowing ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 515.4pt, "high transmittance. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "bold", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(42.6pt, 537.72pt, "2.2.")
  #line-at(58.56pt, 537.72pt, "Photonic-crystal clad ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(51.6pt, 549.84pt, "Photonic crystal (PC) is an artificial periodic structure. The ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 560.28pt, "structure exhibits a PBG effect, where the light with frequency ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 570.6pt, "within the bandgap cannot pass through the structure owing to the ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 580.92pt, "destructive interferences. A lattice of air hole is formed where the ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 591.24pt, "period is approximately half of guided wavelength [10]. Introducing ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 601.68pt, "a line defect creating a guided mode within this bandgap, enabling ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 612pt, "the transmission along the defect. Consequently, PC claddings offer ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 622.32pt, "both wave confinement and mechanical support. Recently, valley ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 632.64pt, "photonic crystal (VPC) waveguides achieve topological protection ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 643.08pt, "by breaking inversion symmetry of the unit cell, which opens a ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 653.4pt, "valley-dependent bandgap [11]. By interfacing two PCs with ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 663.72pt, "opposite valley Chern numbers, a topological edge channel is formed ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 674.04pt, "along the interface. This guided mode exhibits strong suppression of ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 684.36pt, "backscattering, robustness to fabrication deviations, and high ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 694.8pt, "transmission through sharp bends.  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "bold", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(42.6pt, 717.12pt, "2.3.")
  #line-at(58.56pt, 717.12pt, "Effective-medium clad ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(51.6pt, 729.24pt, "Since the PC and VPC waveguides rely on the PBG effect, the ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 739.56pt, "bandwidth is limited by around ~10%. In some applications that ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 750pt, "require higher bandwidth (e.g., communications) the choice of PC-")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 760.32pt, "based is not sufficient. By employing hexagonal lattice similar to that ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 770.64pt, "of PC, the period of air holes is determined to be much smaller than ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 232.08pt, "the guided wavelength. Thus, the effective media can be treated as a ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 242.4pt, "homogeneous material with lower refractive index than that of the ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 252.84pt, "guided core, and the wave is well confined within the core based on ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 263.16pt, "TIR [12]. Additionally, the advantage of effective-medium structure ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 273.48pt, "is the control of the refractive index. By engineering the fill factor of ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 283.8pt, "air, the cladding achieves a tailorable anisotropic permittivity tensor ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 294.24pt, "based on Maxwell–Garnett approximation. The operation bandwidth ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 304.56pt, "of the effective-medium waveguide is ~40%. To further reduce the ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 314.88pt, "evanescent leakage to the effective media, extreme skin-depth ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 325.2pt, "claddings were introduced to manipulate the permittivity tensor for ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 335.64pt, "maximizing the in-plane anisotropy ratio [13], which is potentially ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 345.96pt, "applied for densely integrated devices.  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "bold", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(308.28pt, 368.28pt, "2.4.")
  #line-at(324.24pt, 368.28pt, "Slot-based waveguide  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(317.28pt, 380.4pt, "In previous waveguides, the waves are confined within a high-")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 390.84pt, "index material (silicon). On the other hand, the slot waveguide ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 401.16pt, "confines the wave within a minute air gap sandwiched by a high-")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 411.48pt, "index material. The mechanism is based on the Maxwell equation, ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 421.8pt, "stating that the normal component of the electric flux density must ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 432.24pt, "be continuous at the boundary, i.e., ")
  #line-at(439.2pt, 432.24pt, "𝜀")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(443.16pt, 434.04pt, "ୗ୧")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(449.28pt, 432.24pt, "𝐸")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(454.44pt, 434.04pt, "୬")
  #line-at(458.52pt, 434.04pt, ",")
  #line-at(459.84pt, 434.04pt, "ୗ୧")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(468.48pt, 432.24pt, "= 𝜀")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(481.68pt, 434.04pt, "ୟ୧୰")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(490.8pt, 432.24pt, "𝐸")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(495.96pt, 434.04pt, "୬")
  #line-at(500.04pt, 434.04pt, ",")
  #line-at(501.36pt, 434.04pt, "ୟ୧୰")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(510.48pt, 432.24pt, ". Therefore, ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 443.4pt, "the ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(322.92pt, 443.4pt, "E")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(328.44pt, 443.4pt, "-field right at the silicon-air boundary in the air gap is ~12 ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 453.6pt, "(𝜀")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(315.96pt, 455.76pt, "ୗ୧")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(322.08pt, 453.96pt, "/𝜀")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(330.48pt, 455.76pt, "ୟ୧୰")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(339.6pt, 453.6pt, ")")
  #line-at(343.32pt, 453.96pt, "  times that in silicon. Such slot-based principles were ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 464.4pt, "applied for both out-of-plane and in-plane configurations [14], [15]. ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 474.72pt, "When feeding the waveguide from a metallic hollow waveguide, a ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 485.04pt, "curvature is introduced at the termination of the silicon beam is ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 495.36pt, "employed to reduce the index and impedance mismatches at the ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 505.8pt, "interface while eliminating the conventional tapered spikes, enabling ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 516.12pt, "efficient taperless coupling [16]. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(308.28pt, 540.24pt, "3.")
  #line-at(319.56pt, 540.24pt, "Advances in Terahertz All-silicon Integrated ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 552.96pt, "Components ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(317.28pt, 568.2pt, "Building upon the fundamental dielectric waveguides introduced ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 578.64pt, "earlier, various THz passive devices have been developed to enable ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 588.96pt, "advanced communication, sensing, and imaging functionalities. ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 599.28pt, "These devices leverage low loss and compact features, allowing ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 609.6pt, "scalable integration on all-dielectric substrates. This section ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 620.04pt, "summarizes ")
  #line-at(361.467pt, 620.04pt, "representative ")
  #line-at(422.317pt, 620.04pt, "state-of-the-art ")
  #line-at(486.084pt, 620.04pt, "components ")
  #line-at(539.859pt, 620.04pt, "and ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 630.36pt, "applications, including their designs and operation principles, to ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 640.68pt, "future THz systems.  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "bold", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(308.28pt, 663pt, "3.1.")
  #line-at(324.24pt, 663pt, "Valley photonic crystal triplexer  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(317.28pt, 675.24pt, "The triplexer was developed to (de)multiplex signal on a VPC ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 685.56pt, "platforms to reduce the backscattering with a relatively high ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 695.88pt, "isolation [17]. Starting with a basic bearded interface, the ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 706.2pt, "propagation mode exists in the whole bandgap (320–375 GHz). Then, ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 716.64pt, "a diplexer is developed by employing a frequency filter formed by a ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 726.96pt, "zigzag-interface with a certain distance. By optimizing the size of ")
  #line-at(308.28pt, 737.28pt, "zigzag-interface triangles, the propagation mode exists and the filter ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#0e2841"))
  #line-at(49.92pt, 193.44pt, "Figure 1 Various types of all-dielectric waveguide based on wave confinement mechanisms: (a) all-air clad, (b) photonic-crystal clad, (c) ")
  #line-at(49.92pt, 203.88pt, "effective-medium clad, (d) slot based. Waves propagate along the z-axis. a: lattice constant, ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0e2841"))
  #line-at(383.4pt, 203.88pt, "𝜆")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0e2841"))
  #line-at(387.72pt, 205.68pt, "௚")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#0e2841"))
  #line-at(392.4pt, 203.88pt, ": guided wavelength at central frequency.  ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 7.818pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(472.804pt, 175.443pt, "(d) ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 7.818pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(485.525pt, 175.443pt, "Slot based")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 7.818pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(322.08pt, 175.443pt, "(c) ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 7.818pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(333.842pt, 175.443pt, "Effective-medium clad")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 7.818pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.36pt, 175.443pt, "(a)")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 7.818pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(82.903pt, 175.443pt, " Air-clad")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.822pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
